---
.title = "Use Io.Dir and Io.File Handles",
.date = "2026-09-29",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

`std.Io.Dir` opens paths relative to a directory, while `std.Io.File` represents an open file
handle. Every operation receives the same `std.Io` context. The example writes, closes, reopens,
and reads a temporary file, then removes it.

> 💡 For comprehensive file and directory operations, please see [Create and manage files](file-system/file-operations).

